===Etymology===
Late 17th century, {{bor+|de|nl|frikadel|nocap=1}} (attested 1607), itself from {{der|de|fr|fricadelle|fricadel(le)}}. The French is only recorded in 1742, but its earlier existence is likely as it is a variant of {{m|fr|fricandeau}} (1548), which see. A further relation with {{cog|it|frittatella}} is speculative. Derivation of {{m+|de||Frikadelle}} from Italian instead of Dutch (as suggested in some sources) is implausible in view of the chronology and regional distribution. Compare also {{cog|nl|frikandel}}.

